      "writtenOn": "2022-02-25T17:35:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "See below, I think you should combine the input/output compatible nodes.\n\nThen you can set `#define DT_DRV_COMPAT x96_ap_pwrseq_gpio` and then use `DT_INST_FOREACH_STATUS_OKAY` as the iterator.\n\nI think you can use `DT_INST_NODE_HAS_PROP` to check for an input boolean property.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 11,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 13,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "bd7c7ba41d3e9171aafeccf28e9b8a47b832ee54",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2a75a19a_73721064",
        "filename": "zephyr/subsys/ap_pwrseq/signal_gpio.c",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 47,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-02-25T17:35:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The use of indexes seems pretty fragile - your `int_config` and `spec` arrays are different sizes for example.\n\nI think it would be better to either pass `enum power_signal` everywhere.  This wastes some space as the GPIO, VW, and external drivers all have to allocate sparse arrays.\n\nYou could also have each driver register a list of power signals with `signal_interface.c`.  Then `signal_interface.c` should pass a pointer to the sub-driver\u0027s power signal structure.\n\nSomething like\n```\nvoid power_signal_register(enum power_signal, void *drv_data, ...)\n````\n\n`signal_interface.c` would statically allocate an array that can hold all possible power signal names.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 47,
        "startChar": 33,
        "endLine": 47,
        "endChar": 46
      },
      "revId": "bd7c7ba41d3e9171aafeccf28e9b8a47b832ee54",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "472a79f9_b1b33bbc",
        "filename": "zephyr/subsys/ap_pwrseq/signal_gpio.c",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 128,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-02-25T17:35:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This configures all pins as outputs.  The `spec[]` array contains both inputs and outputs.\n\nI think this would be cleaner if you combined the input/output compatible nodes and added an `input` boolean property to track the input vs. output.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 128,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 128,
        "endChar": 47
      },
      "revId": "bd7c7ba41d3e9171aafeccf28e9b8a47b832ee54",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
